; WaterLilypad1 — 1st of 2 lilypad-dressed Water variants (content-variety pass Task 8,
; 2026-08-26). Sparser of the two: 2 lilypads. See WaterLilypad2.tscn for the denser (4
; lilypad) sibling and water.tres's own header for the model_scenes array change and the
; equal-weight open question this pair raises.
;
; STRUCTURE: instances the existing res://assets/terrain/water/Water.tscn verbatim as a
; child (identity transform — same position/shader/ripple/fresnel treatment as every plain
; water tile, per the task's explicit "don't duplicate the shader setup" instruction) plus
; 2 Lilypad.fbx prop instances scattered near the tile edges. This scene does NOT touch
; Water.tscn or water_surface.gdshader.
;
; Source: "Lilypad.fbx", Ultimate Nature Pack by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — found by
; on-disk `find` in the already-owned pack directory (source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature
; Pack.../FBX/Lilypad.fbx), NOT a poly.pizza standalone download, so this pass extends
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres's assets_used list
; rather than quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres (see that file's own note on this
; discrepancy from the task brief's file list, which named the poly.pizza source before
; the on-disk search confirmed the pack source instead). License.txt re-checked at
; `source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature Pack - Jun 2019.../License.txt` before import, per
; asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate — same boilerplate CC0 1.0 text as every other
; Quaternius pack in this repo. No embedded textures (2 flat vertex-color materials,
; "Green"/"Pink", per the source .mtl) so no texture files to carry over, same as
; Bush.fbx/Rock_Moss_N.fbx's no-texture precedent.
;
; RAW SOURCE LOCATION: copied once to res://assets/terrain/lilypad/Lilypad.fbx (a shared
; per-model directory, NOT duplicated into this scene's own folder) and referenced here by
; uid from both WaterLilypad1.tscn and WaterLilypad2.tscn — same "one raw copy, reused by
; uid across multiple composed scenes" convention RockCluster5.tscn/RockCluster6.tscn
; already established for rock_moss_5/Rock_Moss_5.fbx and rock_moss_2/Rock_Moss_2.fbx,
; chosen over a literal duplicate-per-scene copy (a reasonable reading of the task brief's
; "(+ raw source)" file list, but not what this project's own precedent does for a shared
; single-model source reused by more than one composed scene).
;
; SCALE: raw Lilypad.fbx measured AABB (one-off SceneTree script, same procedure Task 5/6
; used) = size (1.197, 0.221, 1.189) in the file's own baked local space — i.e. a single
; raw lilypad is nearly the FULL 1x1 tile footprint on its own, far too big for a scattered
; edge prop. Scaled down to 0.24 and 0.28 per instance here (~0.29-0.34 footprint each) so
; 2 lilypads read as discrete pads near the tile's edges rather than one giant pad covering
; the tile. FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured GDD number — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: same
; open question every prior prop-scale judgment call in this pass carries, whether the
; lilypad reads at the correct relative size against the water surface and other terrain
; props at the fixed ~45 degree camera pitch.
;
; PLACEMENT: both lilypads positioned toward two opposite corners (not tile-centered, not
; overlapping the water tile's center where a future ripple/reflection focal point might
; sit) — same "props near tile edges" placement Task 5's floor-patch scatter (see e.g.
; Bush.tscn's FloorPatch_N transforms) already demonstrates for a different prop type on a
; different terrain. Y = -0.11, ~0.03 above Water.tscn's own surface plane at y = -0.14, so
; the pads read as resting on the water surface rather than z-fighting or floating detached
; above it.
;
; TILE-BOUNDARY CLEARANCE (CORRECTED 2026-08-26, post-review fix): the original version of
; this scene claimed a "|position| + scale * 0.6 < ~0.44" safety margin — that formula was
; WRONG (it does not correctly account for the raw mesh's actual off-center local AABB, and
; the reviewer's own recomputation of that exact formula got 0.53-0.56, already over the 0.5
; tile half-footprint by the formula's own math). The TRUE worst-case footprint was measured
; by transforming the raw model's actual local AABB corners through each instance's real
; Transform3D (one-off SceneTree script, res://tests/_measure_lilypad_clearance.gd, deleted
; after use — a proper full-corner transform, not a shortcut) and reading off clearance from
; all 4 tile edges (x=+-0.5, z=+-0.5). Original placement measured this way: Lilypad_A
; cleared its nearest edge (x=-0.5) by only 0.00047 units (0.09% of the tile half-width) and
; Lilypad_B cleared its nearest edge (x=+0.5) by only 0.0016 — both technically inside but
; effectively touching the line, not a real safety margin. FIXED by nudging both positions
; ~0.03 units toward tile center (Lilypad_A: (-0.30,-0.11,-0.28) -> (-0.27,-0.11,-0.25);
; Lilypad_B: (0.27,-0.11,0.25) -> (0.24,-0.11,0.22)) — same scale/rotation, only translation
; changed. RE-VERIFIED with the same script: Lilypad_A worst-case clearance is now 0.0305,
; Lilypad_B is now 0.0316 — both genuinely inside the tile with real margin, not by-a-hair.
;
; NO "Slab" WRAPPER NEEDED: unlike every land terrain, Water.tscn's own ground geometry
; already lives under a node named "Slab" inside the instanced Water.tscn itself (see that
; scene's own header — the OcclusionFader exemption mechanism is internal to Water.tscn,
; not something this wrapper scene needs to reproduce). The lilypad props sit as plain
; siblings of the Water instance; if OcclusionFader ever needs to fade them, that is a
; deliberate future call, not an oversight — lilypads are small props, not ground.
[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]

